  "details": "- arm64: errata: Mitigate TLBI errata on various Arm CPUs {CVE-2026-53354}\n- arm64: Add part number for Arm Cortex-A78AE {CVE-2026-53354}\n- PCI: use generic driver_override infrastructure {CVE-2026-53120}\n- driver core: platform: use generic driver_override infrastructure {CVE-2026-31527}\n- tty: port: fix tty_port_tty_vhangup() race {CVE-2026-98752}\n- tty: introduce and use tty_port_tty_vhangup() helper {CVE-2026-98752}\n- mpls: add seqcount to protect the platform_label{,s} pair {CVE-2026-43042}\n- RDMA/srp: bound SRP_RSP sense copy by the received length {CVE-2026-53186}\n- smb: client: reject short READ responses in CIFSSMBRead() {CVE-2026-97565}\n- KVM: arm64: vgic: Check the interrupt is still ours before migrating it {CVE-2026-72289}\n- Input: rmi_smbus - fix out-of-bounds read in rmi_smb_write_block() {CVE-2026-98204}\n- wifi: carl9170: bound memcpy length in cmd callback to prevent OOB read {CVE-2026-68351}\n- clk: scpi: bound-check DVFS index in scpi_dvfs_recalc_rate {CVE-2026-98362}\n- power: supply: core: fix supplied_from allocations {CVE-2026-74271}\n- assoc_array: don't chain a new shortcut onto an existing one",
